\title{AIR}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The arithmetisation the STARK toolkits consume, and the entry point for the formalisation work:
    [Plonky3](dhsorens-003I) and Stwo both take an AIR as input, and [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) targets
    it.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Execution trace, transition constraints, boundary constraints; the uniformity assumption
        that makes the format succinct.}
        \li{Constraint degree, and how it propagates into the quotient polynomial and the
        [rate](dhsorens-002O).}
        \li{Preprocessed columns and randomised AIR with preprocessing (RAP) — what the extra
        randomness is for.}
        \li{Multiple tables and cross-table constraints; how a [zkVM's chips](dhsorens-003T) are
        expressed.}
        \li{Padding, and the soundness bugs that live in the boundary between padded and real rows.}
    }
}
